# Should I still be looking this often when comfortable? And is what I call a jolt still one?
#
# The whole sensing review, as data — TWO re-picks from ONE window of evidence. Note what is
# NOT in it: soil, moisture, plants, or any number this file chose. The thresholds are the
# constitution's, the room is the reviewer's intersection of world and self, and the evidence
# is statistics computable without knowing what a property means — so the same lines would
# serve a society allocating electricity.
#
# `$me`, `$evidence` and `$picks` are the three things a shipped rule cannot know and are
# substituted before it runs. Everything else is discovered. Prefixes come from store.PREFIXES,
# exactly as for a query in Python — a rule must not carry its own.
#
# THE CADENCE (sensing:slowSleepS):
#
#   spread = 0        the instrument did not move AT ALL -> likelier broken than the world is
#                     still, so watch closer, not less
#   spread > steady   it is telling me something -> keep looking
#   otherwise         nothing is happening and unanimously so -> let the board sleep
#
# Relaxing needs every sensor to agree; tightening needs one dissenter. The cost of watching a
# still pot too closely is some battery; the cost of the reverse is a dead plant.
#
# THE JOLT THRESHOLD (sensing:alarmDeltaFraction) — the same evidence, read the other way
# round, because the two watchers trade the vigil between them:
#
#   any spread > steady   the world is lively, so the tight cadence above already carries the
#                         news -> coarsen the delta to the ceiling, or routine liveliness
#                         spends the battery on alarm wakes that tell nobody anything
#   otherwise             the world is still and the cadence above has relaxed, so the ULP
#                         watch is the only watcher left — and a fine delta then costs
#                         NOTHING, because a still value never crosses it -> the floor
#
# One dissenter is enough to coarsen, for the same battery arithmetic as the cadence: the delta
# is the agent's, one twitchy channel wakes the whole board, and the still channels lose only
# sensitivity they were not using. A frozen instrument (spread = 0) takes the floor with the
# still case — a flat line fires no delta whatever its size, and if the instrument revives with
# a jolt, the fine threshold is exactly what reports it at once.
#
# See knowledge/decisions/a-belief-is-a-pick-within-a-range.md.

SELECT ?term ?value WHERE {
  {
    { SELECT (MIN(?s) AS ?lo) (MAX(?s) AS ?hi) (MIN(?n) AS ?least) WHERE {
        GRAPH <$evidence> { ?e a review:Evidence ; review:sampleSpread ?s ; review:sampleCount ?n } } }
    GRAPH ?o { sensing:SensingCapability sensing:steadyFraction ?steady ; sensing:reviewWindow ?window }
    GRAPH <$evidence> { ?r a review:Range ; review:onTerm sensing:slowSleepS ;
                           review:notBelow ?floor ; review:notAbove ?ceiling }
    FILTER(?least >= ?window)
    BIND(sensing:slowSleepS AS ?term)
    BIND(IF(?lo = 0.0 || ?hi > ?steady, ?floor, ?ceiling) AS ?value)
  } UNION {
    { SELECT (MAX(?s) AS ?hi) (MIN(?n) AS ?least) WHERE {
        GRAPH <$evidence> { ?e a review:Evidence ; review:sampleSpread ?s ; review:sampleCount ?n } } }
    GRAPH ?o { sensing:SensingCapability sensing:steadyFraction ?steady ; sensing:reviewWindow ?window }
    GRAPH <$evidence> { ?r a review:Range ; review:onTerm sensing:alarmDeltaFraction ;
                           review:notBelow ?floor ; review:notAbove ?ceiling }
    FILTER(?least >= ?window)
    BIND(sensing:alarmDeltaFraction AS ?term)
    BIND(IF(?hi > ?steady, ?ceiling, ?floor) AS ?value)
  }
}
